meta {
  name: Impersonate - Generic Proxy (example: manager/shifts)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/web-admin/impersonate/{{user_id}}/manager/shifts
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  Generic dispatch contract: any "/web-admin/impersonate/{userId}/{role}/..."
  path forwards in-process to the real role handler for that exact sub-path,
  for GET / POST / PUT / PATCH / DELETE, with the impersonated `{userId}`
  substituted for the Web-Admin caller's own resolved identity.

  This single catch-all route (infra/template.yaml `ImpersonateFunction`
  ProxyAllGet/Post/Put/Patch/Delete events, all on
  `/web-admin/impersonate/{userId}/{proxy+}`) replaces the old per-route
  whitelist — there is no separate registration step for new real routes.

  Request/response shape: identical to calling the real
  `/{role}/...` route directly (e.g. `GET /manager/shifts`), since the real
  handler is invoked unmodified — only the resolved caller identity differs.

  Example equivalent real-traffic routes reachable this way:
    GET    /web-admin/impersonate/{userId}/manager/shifts
    POST   /web-admin/impersonate/{userId}/manager/shifts
    PUT    /web-admin/impersonate/{userId}/manager/shifts/{shiftId}
    DELETE /web-admin/impersonate/{userId}/manager/shifts/{shiftId}
    POST   /web-admin/impersonate/{userId}/manager/schedule/generate
    POST   /web-admin/impersonate/{userId}/manager/schedule/publish
    GET    /web-admin/impersonate/{userId}/manager/schedule/drafts
    GET    /web-admin/impersonate/{userId}/org-admin/shifts
    GET    /web-admin/impersonate/{userId}/employee/shifts
    GET    /web-admin/impersonate/{userId}/manager/employees/{employeeId}/availability
    GET    /web-admin/impersonate/{userId}/{org-admin|manager|employee}/notifications
    PATCH  /web-admin/impersonate/{userId}/{org-admin|manager|employee}/notifications/{notificationId}

  Errors:
    404 - impersonated {userId} does not resolve to a real user
    400 - the "{role}/..." sub-path does not match any registered real route
          (e.g. typo, or a route that genuinely does not exist on that role)
}
